t dead-end alcoves off the main route are hidden collectible coins and reward blocks that reward exploring above and beside the obvious path. Floating brick and question blocks recur at the established blocky scale, used both as ceiling-height obstacles in the low corridors and as stepping supports over pits. The right edge (high x) is the exit, where the path climbs back upward through stepped brick ledges to an upright cylindrical warp pipe (or upward opening) positioned so the player rises out of the cavern and into the adjacent castle_finale stage, whose baseline sits higher up; the exit geometry and surrounding ledges align with that upward transition so the handoff is seamless. The overall reachable route always preserves at least one continuous jumping path from the upper-left entry down through the corridors, across the pits, and up to the right exit, but with the smallest margins and most enclosed geometry of the course so far. Downstream steps choose exact counts, placement, ledge widths, pit gaps, corridor heights, and the specifics of the moving/crumbling platforms, hidden coin pockets, blocks, and the exit climb within this enclosed, rising-difficulty underground segment.

